orrectly. The status LEDs and their series resistors are wired between signal and 3.3 V, so they will not light as intended. Rails and ground are shorted together through this net, which can overload the 3.3 V LDO and the power ground.\", \"confidence\": 0.6}], \"summary\": \"The netlist's ADC3_0_FCC net bridges ground-return pins (including the REG1 feedback bottom resistor R6 and LED return resistors) with 3.3 V pull-ups and decoupling, which the SPICE deck places on node 0 and +3V3 respectively. This likely produces a GND-to-3.3V short and a wrong 5 V feedback reference.\"}",
